cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ltpred, please cite the software and the method(s) used. The references below cover the implemented methods and their direct interpretation."
title: "ltpred: LT-FH, LT-FH++, ADuLT and PA-FGRS genetic-liability estimation in Python"
abstract: >-
  A Python implementation of personalised liability-threshold genetic-liability
  estimation: LT-FH conditions on family history, LT-FH++ adds age-, birth-year-
  and sex-dependent prevalence, ADuLT uses the personalised construction without
  family history, and PA-FGRS contributes deterministic Pearson-Aitken inference
  and an age-censored-control mixture. Inference uses a
  truncated-multivariate-normal Gibbs sampler or deterministic Pearson-Aitken
  approximation, with optional parental-factor quadrature for additive nuclear
  families and pairwise composite-likelihood variance-component fitting.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Vilhjálmsson"
    given-names: "Bjarni Jóhann"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bvilhjal/ltpred"
license: MIT
version: 0.7.0
date-released: "2026-09-16"
keywords:
  - liability-threshold model
  - LT-FH
  - LT-FH++
  - ADuLT
  - PA-FGRS
  - genetic liability
  - family history
  - GWAS
